1
00:00:00,300 --> 00:00:04,340
On the night of October 11, freezers in hundreds of French supermarkets
10月11日夜里，法国几百家超市的冰柜，

2
00:00:04,340 --> 00:00:06,910
were remotely heated to 50 degrees Celsius.
被黑客远程加热到了50度。

3
00:00:06,910 --> 00:00:08,420
That's 122 Fahrenheit.
那是122华氏度。

4
00:00:08,420 --> 00:00:10,600
The ice cream did not survive.
冰淇淋表示：我不干了。

5
00:00:10,600 --> 00:00:12,960
Today's question: a freezer makes cold, right?
今天的问题：冰柜明明是造冷的，

6
00:00:12,960 --> 00:00:14,870
So how do you turn it into an oven?
它怎么能变成烤箱？

7
00:00:14,870 --> 00:00:15,520
Meet Scoop.
认识一下小勺。

8
00:00:15,520 --> 00:00:18,880
Scoop is an ice cream cone, and Scoop is nervous today.
小勺是一个冰淇淋，今天它很紧张。

9
00:00:18,880 --> 00:00:22,570
According to reports, at least 300 Intermarché and Netto stores
据报道，光是英特马歇和奈拓，

10
00:00:22,570 --> 00:00:23,220
were hit.
就至少有300家店中招。

11
00:00:23,220 --> 00:00:25,840
Carrefour said 80 more, plus several other chains.
家乐福说80家，还有好几家连锁也中招。

12
00:00:25,840 --> 00:00:28,160
Some equipment even started to catch fire.
有的设备甚至开始冒火。

13
00:00:28,160 --> 00:00:29,880
One boss estimated the damage:
老板估计：一天之内，

14
00:00:29,880 --> 00:00:32,480
tens of millions of euros, in a single day.
损失几千万欧元。

15
00:00:32,480 --> 00:00:35,420
First, a surprise: a fridge doesn't make cold at all.
先说一个反常识：冰箱根本不会“造冷”。

16
00:00:35,420 --> 00:00:36,320
It moves heat.
它只会搬热。

17
00:00:36,320 --> 00:00:38,000
Like bailing a boat with a sponge:
就像用海绵从船里舀水：

18
00:00:38,000 --> 00:00:40,190
soak it up inside, squeeze it out outside.
在里面吸饱，到外面拧干。

19
00:00:40,190 --> 00:00:42,760
The refrigerant evaporates inside and soaks up heat.
冷媒在柜子里蒸发，吸走热量，

20
00:00:42,760 --> 00:00:46,090
The compressor squeezes it, and the coils outside dump that heat.
压缩机一挤，在外面的管子上把热放掉。

21
00:00:46,090 --> 00:00:48,180
That's why the back of a fridge feels warm.
所以冰箱背后总是热乎乎的。

22
00:00:48,180 --> 00:00:49,460
That's your food's heat.
那是你食物的热。

23
00:00:49,460 --> 00:00:51,780
Twist one: every freezer already has a heater
反转一：每个冰柜里，

24
00:00:51,780 --> 00:00:52,670
built right in.
本来就装着一个加热器。

25
00:00:52,670 --> 00:00:54,950
Freezers grow frost, and the thicker the frost,
因为冷柜会结霜，霜越厚，

26
00:00:54,950 --> 00:00:56,280
the worse they move heat.
搬热就越慢。

27
00:00:56,280 --> 00:00:59,040
So every so often a heater melts the ice away.
所以它定时开一会儿加热，把霜化掉，

28
00:00:59,040 --> 00:01:00,370
It's called defrost.
这叫除霜。

29
00:01:00,370 --> 00:01:03,580
French media reported that's exactly what the attackers did:
据法国媒体报道，黑客做的就是：

30
00:01:03,580 --> 00:01:05,360
forced defrost, and kept it on.
强行除霜，一直不停。

31
00:01:05,360 --> 00:01:08,080
All of this runs on a small connected controller,
控制这一切的，是一个联网的小盒子，

32
00:01:08,080 --> 00:01:10,600
so repair companies can manage it remotely.
好让维修公司远程管理。

33
00:01:10,600 --> 00:01:12,620
Most of the hit units were old models
中招的大多是老型号，

34
00:01:12,620 --> 00:01:14,990
the maker had stopped updating years ago.
厂家早就不再给它们更新。

35
00:01:14,990 --> 00:01:17,380
Twist two: if a freezer simply loses power,
反转二：其实冰柜停电，

36
00:01:17,380 --> 00:01:18,500
it's usually fine.
问题并不大。

37
00:01:18,500 --> 00:01:22,660
The US Department of Agriculture says a full freezer, door closed,
美国农业部说，装满的冰柜关着门，

38
00:01:22,660 --> 00:01:24,360
holds for about 48 hours.
能撑大约48小时。

39
00:01:24,360 --> 00:01:27,260
Because melting ice swallows a lot of heat:
因为冰要化，得先吃进一大口热：

40
00:01:27,260 --> 00:01:29,130
334 joules for every gram.
每克334焦耳。

41
00:01:29,130 --> 00:01:30,370
Ice is a heat sponge.
冰就是一块热量海绵，

42
00:01:30,370 --> 00:01:31,840
It buys your food time.
替食物挡时间。

43
00:01:31,840 --> 00:01:33,830
But a heater cooks it from the inside.
可加热器是从里面往上烤。

44
00:01:33,830 --> 00:01:35,630
No sponge can keep up with that.
海绵再大，也扛不住。

45
00:01:35,630 --> 00:01:37,200
50 degrees is almost as hot
50度，差不多是死亡谷

46
00:01:37,200 --> 00:01:39,420
as Death Valley on its hottest days.
最热那几天的温度。

47
00:01:39,420 --> 00:01:41,750
Twist three: even if the food freezes again,
反转三：就算东西又冻回去了，

48
00:01:41,750 --> 00:01:43,190
it all goes in the trash.
也得全扔。

49
00:01:43,190 --> 00:01:45,810
Between 4 and 60 degrees is the danger zone.
4到60度是危险区，

50
00:01:45,810 --> 00:01:48,320
Bacteria can double in about 20 minutes.
细菌大约20分钟就能翻一倍。

51
00:01:48,320 --> 00:01:50,130
One becomes two, two becomes four.
一个变两个，两个变四个，

52
00:01:50,130 --> 00:01:52,120
In two hours, that's six doublings.
两个小时，翻六次。

53
00:01:52,120 --> 00:01:54,120
Freezing only puts bacteria to sleep.
冷冻只能让细菌睡觉，

54
00:01:54,120 --> 00:01:55,370
It doesn't kill them.
杀不死它们。

55
00:01:55,370 --> 00:01:57,780
So the rule is: two hours in the danger zone,
所以规矩是：在危险区待过两小时，

56
00:01:57,780 --> 00:01:58,760
and out it goes.
就扔掉。

57
00:01:58,760 --> 00:01:59,780
That's why overnight,
这就是为什么一夜之间，

58
00:01:59,780 --> 00:02:01,120
whole shelves went empty.
货架全空了。

59
00:02:01,120 --> 00:02:05,640
One security analyst says stores in Spain, Portugal, Poland, Germany and Belgium
据一位安全分析师说，西班牙、葡萄牙、波兰、德国、比利时

60
00:02:05,640 --> 00:02:06,780
were affected too.
也有超市受影响。

61
00:02:06,780 --> 00:02:09,980
Friendly fine print: so far, officials haven't said who did it,
友情提示：到目前为止，是谁干的、

62
00:02:09,980 --> 00:02:11,060
or how they got in.
怎么进去的，官方都还没说。

63
00:02:11,060 --> 00:02:13,380
France's cyber agency gave simple advice:
法国网络安全部门的建议很朴素：

64
00:02:13,380 --> 00:02:16,620
unplug those boxes from the internet, or lock the door.
把这些盒子从网上断开，或者把门锁好。

65
00:02:16,620 --> 00:02:18,620
Anything you can control from far away,
能远程控制的东西，

66
00:02:18,620 --> 00:02:19,960
someone else might, too.
别人也可能远程控制。

67
00:02:19,960 --> 00:02:21,690
So, your smart gadgets at home?
所以，你家的智能设备，

68
00:02:21,690 --> 00:02:22,810
Keep them updated.
记得更新。

69
00:02:22,810 --> 00:02:25,420
Scoop is fine. Scoop lives in a home freezer.
小勺没事，它在家里的冰箱里。

70
00:02:25,420 --> 00:02:27,390
Yours isn't online... is it?
你家冰箱，没联网吧？

